    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup is headlined by **Zack Gelof** (67.85) and **Bryce Harper** (67.24), who provide our highest offensive ceilings. **Zack Gelof** benefits from a massive 10% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Kikuchi (4.43 xERA), while **Bryce Harper** remains our most consistent anchor against May. **Will Smith** (65.37) also warrants attention; despite facing King, his status in the #3 hole and strong xwOBA metrics make him a high-efficiency play. We are leaning heavily into the platoon edges offered by **Lawrence Butler** and **Zack Gelof** against Kikuchi, though we remain mindful that **Lawrence Butler** is fighting a 13% drag due to a negative platoon split.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Yainer Diaz** (43.85) out of the starting lineup. While his base projection remains respectable, the combination of a tough matchup against Logan Gilbert (3.42 xERA) and a detrimental park factor pushed him below our core starters. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** (39.94) flirted with eligibility but ultimately fell below our 40.0 floor, failing to provide enough projected utility to justify a start in a game where his order slot #9 puts a cap on his counting-stat ceiling.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Justin Crawford** (54.49), whose efficiency is suppressed by an unfavorable #9 lineup position despite a decent matchup against May. While we maintain a robust lineup, we are monitoring the bottom third of our order\u2014specifically **Kyle Karros** and **Justin Crawford**\u2014for any late-breaking lineup changes that might shift these projections. We continue to keep **Braden Montgomery** and **Masyn Winn** in reserve as high-upside depth should the game environment fluctuate before first pitch. **Tyler Freeman** remains in the minors, removing him from consideration entirely for this rotation cycle.",
